{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Jacob answered, etc.</b> One needs to know what the wisdom was that they employed, which Onkelos translates ״בְּחָכְמְתָא״ (\"with wisdom\"), and this is nothing but theft of the mind [i.e., deception]. Further, what is his intention in saying <b>and they spoke because</b>, etc.:" "<b>Indeed,</b> he intends by saying <b>with guile</b> that they contrived not to let Hamor and Shechem sense their cunning — for this is the main thing, since what would their cunning avail if Hamor and Shechem sensed it and took the necessary precautions, or at least would not do the thing that was feared. Therefore they contrived in their reply, and before all else they revealed that they were indignant about the matter, for otherwise the guile would be noticeable, since the deed was known — that such a thing is not done. If they were to conceal their indignation even slightly, it would betray deception. Therefore they opened their words with harsh speech, ״אֲשֶׁר טִמֵּא״ (\"who defiled\"), etc., and this is what is meant by <b>and they spoke</b> — harsh speech, rebuking them for the matter. And thereby they removed the suspicion that they were speaking one thing with the mouth and another in the heart, for they had shown their indignation." "And afterward they spoke to them with soft speech, and this is what is meant by <b>and they said, We cannot</b> — meaning, they were inclined and wished to give her to him, but they could not give her to one <b>who has a foreskin</b>. And they did not say ״אֲשֶׁר הוּא עָרֵל״ (\"who is uncircumcised\"), because for that argument it would suffice if he himself circumcised the flesh of his foreskin. Therefore they said <b>who has a foreskin</b> — meaning, who has the license of a foreskin, for what difference would it make if he himself circumcised, while the children born to him from Dinah would remain uncircumcised, since they have no obligation of circumcision?" "Further, they gave a reason in their words, that the main thing was in order that they intermarry with them and take wives one from another and become one people — and this would not come about unless all were circumcised. Therefore they said <b>Only on this condition will we consent to you</b>, etc. <b>that every male be circumcised.</b> They were precise in saying ״אַךְ״ (\"only\") to exclude the argument that Hamor accept circumcision upon himself and his seed, for that would not suffice for the reason we have written, but rather specifically <b>that every male among you be circumcised.</b> And their ultimate intention is, of course, hidden among them — to kill them all, with none to save from their hand. Further, they contrived to remove from them any suspicion of guile in every single statement they made to them, as I shall explain immediately, with the help of HaShem blessed be He."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:00.942920995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}